From bb31b45d5d19fdd54a1500e96459b9b32c98610c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 23:28:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/23] gated_delta_net : add chunked prefill kernel (opt-in,
 correct but slow)

Implement the chunked gated delta rule for prefill (S_v=128, scalar gates,
K=1): phase A builds the per-chunk closure matrix, k_cumsum/k_cumdecay and
attn_causal; phase B propagates the state chunk by chunk over V-slices.

aiter's chunk_gated_delta_rule_fwd_h.cu does not run on gfx1201 (its own test
skips gfx12), so this is our own f32 implementation, validated in python
against the op recurrence. Enabled via GGML_CUDA_GDN_CHUNKED=1 only: it is
correct (45/45 backend-ops tests on both paths, PPL 6.30 vs 6.26, generation
matches) but currently slower than the sequential kernel (pp512 4200 vs 5925)
because the phase-A matmuls are untiled. Add 4 S_v=128 prefill cases to the
test-backend-ops eval set.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
